      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "CANYA TALK NOW (1) has been in the minors the last two, the latest showing strong pace early but gathered in and finished a 1.2 lengths second over 525m The Meadows in 29.72. Has a very good strike-rate from this draw, with two wins from three starts. Racing well and deserves a win. MEPUNGA REWARD (8) wasn't far away at the finish when 4th and beaten only 3.5 lengths (29.89) at The Meadows. Form here at the trip excellent including six wins. Has a strong record out of this box with five wins and two minor placings from nine starts. Will give the top chances plenty to think about. BABY FACE BANDIT (2) won again in another strong performance after running them ragged to make it two in a row at this track over 515m (29.74). One of the leading chances again. ASTON AQUITAINE (3) recorded a 1.3 lengths win (25.16) in a Grade 4/5 last time at Ballarat. Has already won out of this draw.",
